<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-POOL-V9>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-POOL-V9" ;
  triage:title "control_path_pool is a third, separate pool for roster/graft-lease/nudge/template/peer-config reads and writes; the target design is exactly one serial writer queue plus one capped read pool, with no separate reader lanes" ;
  triage:description "fenix, writer-side pool read audit (01M1T3E38ZRWKTH14X9MK868T1), V9. SharedDb::with_connection/with_transaction (shared_db.rs:212) are the only debug_assert_blocking_only callers, both invoked from control_path_pool on the writer side (blocking). Production ReaderPool lanes today: 'mailbox' (mailbox_reader.rs:41) and 'search' (search_reader.rs:32) only; a 'doctor' lane exists only in test config (DEFAULT_DOCTOR_READER_CONFIG), no production doctor/diagnostics reader lane exists. control_path_pool's module doc declares a design exemption treating roster/graft-lease/nudge/template/peer-config state as 'bounded low-volume control state' served on the writer side for both reads and writes. RULING (Rand, relayed by fenix, msg 01M1T3GRDS1G9W1AWMCRBSA5VX, verbatim): 'the target design is exactly two things. One serial writer queue for every mutation. One read connection pool of N for every read, reads run in parallel; agents may use all N, tool-class reads (peek/search/doctor/diagnostics) capped at a fraction of N. No control-path pool, no separate reader lanes.' This overrules control_path_pool's stated exemption entirely: it must be deleted, along with the mailbox/search/doctor lane split, and replaced with one read pool serving every read (agent-class uncapped, tool-class -- peek/search/doctor/diagnostics -- capped strictly below the pool's full size). Every remaining control_path_pool write moves to the single writer queue. This finding is the architectural precondition the AW-POOL-V1/V3/V4/V5/V7/V8 fixes route their relocated reads and writes into; fix-round acceptance criteria should be worded as subtraction (remove the pool/lane types) rather than addition." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "step2_verdict" ;
  triage:category "architecture-boundary" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-06T01:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AWWriterPoolAudit ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T23:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-POOL-V9/shared-db> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-POOL-V9/control-path-pool> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

